    "value": "The main changes in `io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus` 1.13.0 are quite significant, especially related to Prometheus client library use and package/class names:\n\n### Key Changes (Micrometer 1.13.0):\n\n#### 1. **Upgraded Prometheus Java Client (0.x → 1.x)**\n- `micrometer-registry-prometheus` now builds on the Prometheus Java Client **1.x** (previously 0.x).\n- This upgrade brings breaking changes for anyone using the internal API (e.g., `PrometheusMeterRegistry`), but most frameworks, such as Spring Boot, have adjusted their integrations accordingly.\n- If you have custom code using the Prometheus MeterRegistry API or low-level Prometheus Java objects, **you likely need to make changes.**\n\n#### 2. **New Compatibility Module (Temporary Fallback)**\n- To help projects that can’t immediately migrate, a **new module** exists:  \n  `micrometer-registry-prometheus-simpleclient`\n- This continues to use the **old Prometheus 0.x client** but is **deprecated**. It is meant as a stop-gap only until code can be ported to work with Prometheus 1.x【3:0†source】.\n\n#### 3. **Package \u0026 Type Name Changes**\n- If your code has imports like:\n  ```java\n  import io.micrometer.prometheus.PrometheusConfig;\n  import io.micrometer.prometheus.PrometheusMeterRegistry;\n  ```\n  Change them to:\n  ```java\n  import io.micrometer.prometheusmetrics.PrometheusConfig;\n  import io.micrometer.prometheusmetrics.PrometheusMeterRegistry;\n  ```\n- If you reference Prometheus internal types like `io.prometheus.client.CollectorRegistry`, you should now use `io.prometheus.metrics.model.registry.PrometheusRegistry`【3:5†source】.\n\n#### 4. **Migration Guidance**\n- See the [Micrometer 1.13 Migration Guide](https://github.com/micrometer-metrics/micrometer/wiki/1.13-Migration-Guide) for concrete API changes.\n- Typical build file update:\n  ```gradle\n  // Before\n  runtimeOnly 'io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus:1.12.x'\n  // After\n  runtimeOnly 'io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus:1.13.0'\n  ```\n\n#### 5. **Spring Boot Considerations**\n- Prefer letting Spring Boot BOM manage versions to avoid dependency conflicts.\n- If you're pinning Micrometer/Prometheus versions, validate using integration and actuator endpoints after the upgrade【3:0†source】.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**  \n- `micrometer-registry-prometheus` now uses Prometheus Java client 1.x, which is a breaking change for some use cases.\n- Deprecated fallback module: `micrometer-registry-prometheus-simpleclient`.\n- Package names and key class names have changed.\n- Consult the 1.13 migration guide if you use internal APIs or custom integrations【3:0†source】【3:5†source】【3:4†source】.  \n\nIf you need a detailed list of class/method removals/additions in the 1.13.0 JAR, let me know!",
